    "id": "train-1788",
    "question": "Mr. Shaefer harvested 500 lychees in a carton and took them to the market. He sold half of them and took home the remaining number of lychees where they ate 3/5 of them. Calculate the number of lychees remaining.",
    "gold": "100",
    "answer": "At the market, Mr. Shaefer sold half of the lychees, which is 1/2*500 = 250\nThe remaining number of lychees is 500-250 = <<500-250=250>>250\nAt home, they ate 3/5*250 = <<3/5*250=150>>150 lychees.\nThe total number of lychees remaining is 250-150 = <<250-150=100>>100\n#### 100"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine the number of lychees remaining, we will follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the number of lychees sold.\n2. Determine the number of lychees taken home.\n3. Calculate the number of lychees eaten.\n4. Find the number of lychees remaining.\n\nStep 1: Calculate the number of lychees sold.\nMr. Shaefer sold half of the 500 lychees.\n\\[\n\\text{Number of lychees sold} = \\frac{500}{2} = 250\n\\]\n\nStep 2: Determine the number of lychees taken home.\nThe remaining number of lychees is the total minus the number sold.\n\\[\n\\text{Number of lychees taken home} = 500 - 250 = 250\n\\]\n\nStep 3: Calculate the number of lychees eaten.\nThey ate \\(\\frac{3}{5}\\) of the 250 lychees.\n\\[\n\\text{Number of lychees eaten} = \\frac{3}{5} \\times 250 = 150\n\\]\n\nStep 4: Find the number of lychees remaining.\nThe number of lychees remaining is the number taken home minus the number eaten.\n\\[\n\\text{Number of lychees remaining} = 250 - 150 = 100\n\\]\n\nThus, the number of lychees remaining is \\(\\boxed{100}\\).",
